Program Bug_2_65_ToggleBit_ConstantDoublePass;
// Bug 2.65: Methods6502::ToggleBit (methods6502.cpp ~6503-6546) emits its
// fast constant-bit-index and/ora directly when parameter 1 (the bit
// index) is a compile-time constant, but never `return`s afterward:
// execution falls straight through into the generic path, which
// re-evaluates the bit index through BitShiftX (a runtime shift loop
// building the identical bitmask) and performs the same and/ora again.
// Harmless at runtime (toggling the same bit the same way twice is a
// no-op), so this can't be caught by a value assertion - the final byte
// is correct either way. Verified instead via a static check on the
// generated .asm (see the companion .asmcheck file): BitShiftX's
// "shiftbit"/"shiftbitdone" labels are only ever emitted from that one
// function, so their presence proves the generic runtime path ran even
// though the bit index here is the literal constant 2. GetBit
// (methods6502.cpp ~6549) has the same constant/variable split for
// reading a bit but doesn't have this problem: its constant branch ends
// with a `return;` its ToggleBit counterpart is missing.
var
	flags : byte = %00000000;

begin
	togglebit(flags,2,1);
	loop();
end.
